#. engine/messages/storey_titles.py (ticket 19b): the storeys a sheet's title names against those its plans' titles name. A sheet's storeys are its plans' lists together (docs/data-model.md §3.2), as the engine reads them (S15-E3: no word here promises a storey edit Step 1 does not have).
msgid "engine.storey_titles.differ"
msgstr "{named, select, title {The sheet titled “{sheet}”} other {The title of {sheet}}} names “{stated}”, but its plans do not agree: {not_drawn, plural, =0 {} one {# storey in the title has no plan} other {# storeys in the title have no plan}}{not_drawn, plural, =0 {} other {{not_named, plural, =0 {} other {, and }}}}{not_named, plural, =0 {} one {# storey on a plan is not in the title} other {# storeys on the plans are not in the title}}. Vextrus takes the storeys from its plans."

#. engine/messages/storey_titles.py (T-W318): Step 1's one Question per Discipline over the sheets whose title names storeys their plans do not agree with; the first such sheet is named as the example, with its counts as `differ` gives them. The QS's answer is recorded only: no sheet or plan changes (S15-E3).
msgid "engine.storey_titles.differs"
msgstr "{count, plural, one {The title of 1 sheet names storeys its plans do not agree with:} other {The titles of # sheets name storeys their plans do not agree with, for example,}} {named, select, title {the sheet titled “{sheet}”} other {{sheet}}}, which names “{stated}” ({not_drawn, plural, =0 {} one {# storey in the title has no plan} other {# storeys in the title have no plan}}{not_drawn, plural, =0 {} other {{not_named, plural, =0 {} other {, and }}}}{not_named, plural, =0 {} one {# storey on a plan is not in the title} other {# storeys on the plans are not in the title}}). Vextrus takes the storeys from the plans."
